---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { installUrl, rpcPluginUrl, route } from '../lib/release';
---

<Page title="Setup guide">
  <article class="reading shell">
    <h1>Setup guide</h1>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Install <a href="https://violentmonkey.github.io/get-it/"
          >Violentmonkey</a
        >, or a compatible userscript manager.
      </li><li>
        Open the <a href={installUrl}>Track Control userscript</a> and confirm Install.
        If you see source code instead, use your manager’s “Install from URL” option
        with the download link.
      </li><li>
        Reload SoundCloud and choose a track. Use the tempo controls in the
        bottom player. On your first visit, choose a slider, dial or vertical
        slider.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <section id="desktop">
      <h2>soundcloud-rpc desktop app</h2>
      <p>
        Use the <a href={rpcPluginUrl} download="soundcloud_tempo_control.js"
          >desktop plugin</a
        >, not the browser userscript. Press F1 in the app, open Plugins → Open
        folder, and put <code>soundcloud_tempo_control.js</code> there. Refresh the
        list, enable Track Control, then reload SoundCloud.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keep soundcloud-rpc’s separate Playback Speed plugin disabled. Both
        plugins would try to control the same audio element.
      </p>
      <p>
        Download and replace that same file for future updates. Disabling the
        plugin reloads SoundCloud to remove its audio hooks and interrupts
        playback. Start a track after the controls appear; this wrapper loads
        plugins after the page.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Playback speed</h2><p>
        The slider goes from 0.25× to 2× in 0.025× steps. Type an exact value
        for up to 4×. Double-click the number or slider to reset to 1×;
        Shift-click the arrows for 0.01× adjustments.
      </p><p>
        Use the bookmark button to remember a track’s speed. The gear opens
        settings, saved tracks and the tempo editor.
      </p><p>
        Choose a slider, dial or vertical slider under Appearance. Saved tempos
        apply when you return to a track; turn off “Apply saved tempos” to start
        each track at 1× instead.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id="sharing">
      <h2>Share tempo settings</h2><p>
        Open the tempo editor and choose Copy link. It includes the track, tempo
        points, pitch points, fades and pitch mode. The link opens a player with
        those settings, so the recipient can listen without the plugin when the
        full track is available. Installation is optional for listening on
        SoundCloud itself.
      </p><p>
        For everyday sharing, enable “Include tempo in copied links” in
        settings. Then copying the current, loaded track’s full SoundCloud link
        can include your adjustments. Unloaded tracks and short links may stay
        unchanged.
      </p><p>
        That page also offers the original track without adjustments. Opening a
        tempo link does not automatically play audio or overwrite saved
        settings.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id="limits">
      <h2>Pitch modes</h2><p>
        Natural lets pitch follow speed. Preserve key keeps the original pitch
        as you speed up or slow down a track.
      </p><p>
        Key shift moves the song up or down by up to 12 semitones. Set it in the
        Pitch control beside the tempo slider, Advanced audio or the tempo
        editor. It needs access to the player's audio; with Preserve key, the
        chosen shift stays independent of playback speed.
      </p><p>
        The arrows move in half-semitone steps by default. Type a finer value,
        or change the default increment and range under Advanced audio →
        Semitone controls. Appearance lets you hide the player’s semitone
        control and set the default tempo increment for arrows and keyboard
        adjustments.
      </p><p>
        To change pitch during a song, open the tempo editor and choose Pitch.
        Add points, set their times and choose how they fade into each other.
        Apply once previews the curve; Save timeline keeps it for that track.
        Changing the player’s Pitch control overrides the pitch curve until you
        reapply the timeline.
      </p><p>
        Extreme changes can affect sound quality. Start with small adjustments.
      </p>
      <details class="feature-details">
        <summary
          >Audio processing details<Icon name="chevron" size={18} /></summary
        >
        <p>
          Preserve key uses Signalsmith when Track Control can process the
          player's audio, otherwise it uses the browser's pitch correction.
          Processing adds latency. Output level applies to both pitch modes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Waveform uses SoundCloud's volume envelope. Its time marks show
          minutes and seconds, not detected beats.
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Where things are stored</h2><p>
        Settings and saved timelines stay in SoundCloud’s local site storage in
        this browser. Export a backup from settings before clearing browser
        data.
      </p><a href={route('privacy/')}>Privacy details</a>
    </section>
    <section id="troubleshooting">
      <h2>If something isn’t working</h2>
      <p>
        Missing controls? Check that Track Control is enabled in your userscript
        manager, then reload SoundCloud. Disable older copies of the script.
      </p>
      <p>
        For audio problems, switch off WASM in settings to use the browser's
        pitch correction. If a website preview fails to load, choose Retry, load
        an audio file or use the synth sample.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Page>
